<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lands of the Crown of Saint Stephen</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lands of the Hungarian Crown</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-crown-of-hungary">Crown of Saint Stephen</a> were the territories joined to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> under its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-of-thorns">Holy Crown</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a> and, at times, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>. The idea of the crown as the bearer of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> bound these lands to the Hungarian king while they kept their own institutions, such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatian-parliament">Croatian Sabor</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Compromise of 1867</a> they formed the Hungarian half of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>, until its break-up in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lands-of-the-crown-of-saint-stephen.jpg" alt="Lands of the Crown of Saint Stephen" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hungary_(1915-1918;_angels).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
